{{also|acadèmic}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|academick||obsolete}}
* {{alter|en|acad|acad.||abbreviation}}
* {{alter|en|Academic}}

===Etymology===
From both the {{der|en|ML.|acadēmicus}} and the {{der|en|fr|académique}}, from {{der|en|la|academia}}, from {{der|en|grc|ἀκαδημικός}}, from {{m|grc|Ἀκαδημία}} or {{m|grc|Ἀκαδήμεια}}, the name of the place where Plato taught; compare {{m|en|academy}}.<ref name=WI3>{{R:MW3 1976}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌækəˈdɛmɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-academic.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛmɪk|s=4}}
<!-- 4 syllable words !-->

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Belonging to the school or philosophy of [[Plato]] {{defdate|from late 16th century}}<ref name=SOED/>
#: {{co|en|the '''academic''' sect or philosophy}}
# Belonging to an [[academy]] or other higher institution of learning, or a scholarly society or organization. {{defdate|from late 16th century}}<ref name=SOED/>
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1761|author=w:William Warburton|title=A Charge to the Clergy of the Diocese of Gloucester|title2=The Works of the Right Reverend William Warburton, D.&nbsp;D., Lord Bishop of Gloucester|volume2=9|year2=1811|page2=372|pageurl2=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=fFIJAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA372|text=But unhappily, by too short a view of things, you have been apt to mistake the completion of your '''academic''' courses for the completion of your theologic studies: and then, by a false modesty, have despaired of knowing more than you would suffer those august places of your education to teach you.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|month=December|author=John Alves|title=Resorts for Railfans - 29: Oxford|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=596|text=It was left to the motor industry, half a century later, to destroy Oxford's '''academic''' calm.}}
# In particular: relating to [[literary]], [[classical]], or [[artistic]] studies like the [[humanities]], rather than to [[technical]] or [[vocational]] studies like [[engineering]] or welding.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1991|author=Wisconsin State Board of Vocational, Technical and Adult Education|title=Accountability Report, and ... State Plan for Vocational, Technical and Adult Education in Wisconsin|page=16
|text=Programs of work should provide students the opportunities to demonstrate both '''academic''' and vocational competence attainment.}}
# Having [[little]] [[practical]] [[use]] or [[value]], as by being overly [[detailed]] and [[unengaging]], or by being [[theoretical]] and [[speculative]] with no practical [[importance]]. {{defdate|from late 19th century}}
#: {{cot|en|abstract|artificial}}
#: {{ux|en|I have always had an '''academic''' interest in hacking.}}
#: {{co|en|the distinction is '''academic'''}}
#: {{co|en|an '''academic''' question}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=25 February 1965|author=w:Civil Aeronautics Board|title=Aircraft Accident Report: Pan American World Airways, Inc Boeing 707-121, N709PA, Near Elkton, Maryland, December 8, 1963|chapter=Analysis|url=https://asn.flightsafety.org/reports/1963/19631208_B701_N709PA.pdf|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241201161802/https://asn.flightsafety.org/reports/1963/19631208_B701_N709PA.pdf|archivedate=1 December 2024|accessdate=1 December 2024|page=11|text=The exact sequence and timing of the subsequent explosions and inflight fires are not known and are, in fact, somewhat '''academic''' with respect to the probable cause of the accident.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=But almost always such words are irreversibly established before the objectors learn of their existence, and the objections are hardly more than '''academic''' exercises.|page=112|title=The English Language|author=Robert Burchfield|authorlink=Robert Burchfield|publisher=Oxford University Press|location=Oxford|year=1985}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1985|title=Depyrogenation|page=33
|passage=In theory, a fully intact reverse osmosis membrane should be capable of removing lipopolysaccharide pyrogens {{...}} In practice, this distinction is '''academic''', because pyrogens do not replicate, and as long as the product water is {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990|author=David George Lowe; I. J. M. Jeffrey|title=Surgical Pathology Techniques|publisher=Mosby Incorporated
|text=In practice this distinction is '''academic''', as any small nodule on the surface of a thyroidectomy specimen should be examined histologically. If carcinoma is suspected or proven, the whole surface of the specimen may be marked{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Pakistan's AQ Khan: My Nuclear Manifesto| work=Newsweek| date=May 16, 2011| passage=The question of how many weapons are required for credible deterrence against India is purely '''academic'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Land Rover Discovery review – SUV's the finest car in the Landy| work=Scottish Daily Record| date=Nov 10, 2017| passage=For the majority of owners, its four-wheel-drive endeavours will be of purely '''academic''' interest.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|date=May 22 2018|publisher=US Government Accountability Office|title=Decision, Matter of Sikorsky Aircraft Corporation
|passage=As a general matter, we will not consider a protest where the issue presented has no practical consequences with regard to an existing federal government procurement, and thus is of purely '''academic''' interest.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/ideas/archive/2018/09/the-crisis-of-the-american-elites/571060/|title=The Crisis of the American Elites|work=The Atlantic|date=2018-09-23|author=Eliot A. Cohen|passage={{...|If you are a liberal, you probably do not know or care that Whelan writes often for ''National Review'' and is a leading figure in conservative legal circles}}; if you do not know, or care to know, much about critical theory, the writings of Butler are '''academic''' in the unflattering sense of that term. But in their world, they are, if not royalty, lords of the realm.}}
# Having a [[love]] of or [[aptitude]] for learning.
#: {{ux|en|I’m more '''academic''' than athletic — I get lower marks in phys. ed. than in anything else.}}
